// Pull request author: Diablo-research
// Change: new rule
// Title: LockScreenContentServer Execution From Uncommon Folder
// Sigma ID: b1727dfa-1d70-4a70-b626-00aa3864ed95
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Nazar Diachok (@Diablo-research)
// Date: 2026-09-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects execution of the legitimate Microsoft binary LockScreenContentServer.exe from outside
//   expected Windows directories. Threat actors associated with the TerminalFix campaign copied the
//   binary alongside a malicious dui70.dll under ProgramData to perform DLL sideloading.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative or security testing that copies the binary outside default Windows folders
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/08/28/terminalfix-campaign-deploys-reverse-tunnel-through-multistage-intrusion/
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2025/08/21/think-before-you-clickfix-analyzing-the-clickfix-social-engineering-technique/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cd801b78bc56e7c2f301d0e8282f6e256b7bbe0a/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lockscreencontentserver_uncommon_path.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\LockScreenContentServer.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "LockScreenContentServer.exe") and (not((FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\WinSxS\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\SystemApps\\")))
